SUMMARY:Apollo Works in Process: In Place of Monuments 
LOCATION:The Apollo's Jonelle Procope Theater\, Harlem (South)
DESCRIPTION:Apollo Works in Process In Place of Monuments centers the frien
 
dship of two Black American and Caribbean friends\, examining how state san
 
ctioned violence threatens to tear their family and community apart. Throug
 
h recalling memories across time\, and incorporating movement and dance\, t
 
he play aims to create a portal for audiences to envision more just and lib
 
erated futures for Black and Brown people. The play will be devised in comm
 
unity through a series of workshops writing\, somatic/dance\, readings\, st
 
ory circles\, wardrobe design etc.). The staged reading of the one-act will
 
 be followed by a talkback with the creatives." Tickets & info: https://www
 
.ticketmaster.com/apollo-works-in-process-in-place-new-york-new-york-11-06-
 
2026/event/00006519DF8B9C86
URL:https://www.ticketmaster.com/apollo-works-in-process-in-place-new-york-
 
new-york-11-06-2026/event/00006519DF8B9C86
END:VEVENT
